    "reflection_en": "Recognising another person's wrongdoing does not automatically settle what our own response should be. Arjuna calls them aggressors and still worries about the moral cost of killing them. Ethical clarity requires more than identifying who is wrong; it also requires examining what we ourselves are about to do.",
